My first was like 130-160k turns.  I average 35k now.  Never altar
camp, you don't need to be that overprepared--sometimes it's worth
sac'ing for a weapon, but I spent forever just camping for more
weapons, spellbooks, etc and it's pointless.

Keep a stash on sokoban and use levelport/Eye/etc to get there.  Don't
be afraid to keep all your ?teleport and curse them once you have a big
stack.  That and telecontrol speed things up.

Find a fast way through gehennom: buy clairvoyance at a minimum.
?magic mapping are cheap with a marker, so if you have the wish to burn
do that (and remember lots of wishes, like GoDex, any weapon, most
scrolls, are wastes).  The mapping spell if you can (and remember
confused ?charging restores Pw).  Demon-mapping works well.

Don't feel a need to explore every level completely, especially in
Gehennom: when you've got plenty of stuff, go ahead and ascend.  Yeah
you might be missing a cool death drop or something--do you need it?
If not, why waste all that time?



